	(text "Solartron 7075 opto-isolated USB interface"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8ad14296-3502-5d16-a9b0-ddacef4b394c")
	)
	(text "Signals crossing the isolation barrier (3 x HCPL-2631 dual 10 MBd optocouplers):\n   SCK    MCU -> DVM side   shift clock for both register chains (rising edge shifts)\n   MOSI   MCU -> DVM side   command bits into 2 x TPIC6C595 (16 open-drain outputs)\n   LATCH  MCU -> DVM side   low = load 5 x 74HCT165 (40 inputs); rising edge = update command outputs\n   OEn    MCU -> DVM side   low = enable command outputs (high / LED off = all released)\n   MISO   DVM side -> MCU   status / BCD data out of the 74HCT165 chain\n   DRDY   DVM side -> MCU   PRINT command level (SKB pin 34): high = reading complete, data valid\n\nPower: USB VBUS -> AP2112K-3.3 (MCU side).  VBUS -> ferrite -> isolated 1 W DC-DC (9 V) -> L78M05 -> +5V_ISO\n(the 50-way connector has no supply pin, so the isolated logic is powered across the barrier).\n\nMechanical: 116 x 50 mm, 4 layers.  J1 (DD-50 plug) is on the bottom side, everything else on the top side;\nthe board is held by two 4-40 UNC screws through J1's flange holes into the jackposts of SKB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
